From ee7bd5477d7837e1bf1818502a41d951f4d851cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(redact): mask random-token secret fields and subprocess
 argv in tool output [daveey]

Managed-worker adoption secrets (worker-outboxes/*/pending.json scope.secret,
secrets.token_urlsafe(32)) reached agent transcripts three ways, because
terminal/execute_code output runs code_file=True and skips every key pass:
a printed scope repr, the raw JSON journal, and TimeoutExpired/
CalledProcessError text echoing an argv that carried the secret.

- code_file mode now masks credential-named JSON/repr fields whose value is
  a random token (32+ base64url chars, both cases); fixtures stay intact
  (2 of 20,549 repo files change, both secret canaries).
- every mode masks random tokens inside 'Command [...] timed out after /
  returned non-zero exit status / died with' diagnostics, linear on hostile
  input (tail-anchored bounded backward head search).
- every mode: _JSON_FIELD_ESCAPED_RE starts only at the head of a backslash run
  (it was quadratic on long runs, now reached on default paths); argv tokens
  after = (--token=S, KEY=S) and multi-line shell scripts are masked.
- docs: never pass credentials in argv.

No change to session_worker _claim/_verify. Tests: terminal_tool and
execute_code entry paths (repr, JSON cat, TimeoutExpired), 300 random
token_urlsafe samples, negatives, hostile-input timing.
